{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"01f4100c6dabf72cb5f905875be68734e4103afa79e76b1414237170742927db","digest":{"component_or_area":"rebar_reconciler rich-text cutover test infrastructure","key_entities":["tests/integration/rebar_reconciler/test_reconcile_roundtrip.py::_load_module","sys.modules[\"rebar_reconciler.adapters.jira.adf\"]","AdfCodec","rich_text_codec.py","test_cloud_functions_degrade_without_marklas","test_by_path_loader_preserves_module_identity_for_the_same_source"],"problem_keywords":["module identity","state leakage","sys.modules","test ordering","rich text","codec","fixture isolation"],"propositions":["The integration fixture _load_module unconditionally replaces sys.modules[\"rebar_reconciler.adapters.jira.adf\"] with a fresh module object, causing AdfCodec to retain a stale reference to the prior module object","When test_cloud_functions_degrade_without_marklas runs after the integration fixture in serial ordering, it monkeypatches the wrong module object while AdfCodec.to_wire continues calling the original cached module, causing rich-text assertions to fail","The fixture violates the documented test-infrastructure invariant that canonical dotted keys must preserve module identity across test execution","Caching the module by both canonical name and __file__ source path restores the identity contract while preserving intentional isolation for different-source replacements under the same name"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787411170309007001,"uuid":"44f54ae0-c397-4a78-8248-2a84c34959f1"}